From c2aab13b7479dfd2391dd193a2940720f6df1eed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy J Fontaine <tjfontaine@atxconsulting.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 19:51:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] bifrost: structured LOAD_PROG layout parser with failure
 detail

The bounded LOAD_PROG parser now produces a LoadProgLayout struct
containing payload-relative offsets (maps, instructions, relocs),
parsed counts, and extracted trailer scratch buffers. The dispatch
in bifrost.rs consumes the layout exclusively; the trailer
extraction and offset re-derivation that previously lived inline
are gone. Eliminates the class of bugs where parser and dispatch
could disagree on byte boundaries.

The op=9 LOAD_PROG completion event now carries an optional UTF-8
detail string on the wire (u32 op, u64 seq, i32 status, u16
detail_len, [u8] detail). The kfunc reloc resolver threads the
missing-kfunc name through complete_load_prog_with_detail so the
host CLI can render the specific failure instead of a bare errno.

BIFROST_TRACING_LINK_OPS gets a HACK(upstream-able) marker
describing the one-line fix to bpf_link_init's WARN_ON that would
let the all-None stub go away.

Closes goal items 8 (parser/dispatch coupling), 9 wire-format
follow-up, and 14 (upstream-able workaround marker).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
